# Source archives only.
#
# The parent .htaccess gives every .gz and .zip a one year immutable cache.
# That is right for an installer and wrong here: immutable means the CDN keeps
# the first copy it ever saw, so publishing a broken tarball once leaves every
# visitor getting it while the origin looks perfect and any check that uses a
# cache buster passes. That happened. A source archive is rebuilt from a tag by
# a script, so it is exactly the kind of thing that can be wrong on the first go.
#
# Written as FilesMatch on purpose. A plain Header here loses to the parent's
# FilesMatch no matter that this file is a directory deeper, because Apache
# merges section directives after plain ones. Section against section, the
# child wins.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(gz|zip|txt)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=3600"
    Header unset Expires
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
